"""
Regression test: nethermind block state gas accumulator bug.

63 EVM fuzz transactions from BAL devnet-3 block 17 that expose
a block-level state gas accounting error. The block header
gas_used = max(block_regular_gas, block_state_gas) is exactly
131,488 (= 112 * cost_per_state_byte = GAS_NEW_ACCOUNT) lower
than the EELS reference.

Nethermind undercounts new-account state gas in the block state
gas accumulator. The bug requires the specific fuzz bytecodes —
simple nested-CREATE tests do not trigger it.

Cannot be simplified further: removing any single transaction
eliminates the divergence. All 63 contribute cumulative state.

Tests for [EIP-8037: State Creation Gas Cost Increase]
(https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-8037).
"""

import pytest
from execution_testing import (
    Alloc,
    Block,
    BlockchainTestFiller,
    Environment,
    Fork,
    Transaction,
)

from .spec import ref_spec_8037

REFERENCE_SPEC_GIT_PATH = ref_spec_8037.git_path
REFERENCE_SPEC_VERSION = ref_spec_8037.version


